**Given:**

Sara can finish a work = 18 days

Tara can finish a work = 15 days

**Formula used:**

Work = Efficiency × Time

**Calculation:**

Let the Sara can finish the remaining work in X days.

One day work of Sara = {1over18}

One day work of Tara = {1over15}

Tara worked for 10 days = {10over15}={2over3}

The remaining work = {1-{2over3}}={3-2over3}={1over3}

⇒ X = {{1over3}over{1over18}}={18over3}=6 days

**∴ The required result will be 6 days.**

**Given:**

The expression = sqrt{2+sqrt{2+sqrt{2+2cos8θ}}}

**Formula used:**

1 + cosθ = 2cos²(θ/2)

**Calculation:**

According to the question

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2+sqrt{2+2cos8θ}}}

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2+sqrt{2({1+cos8θ})}}}

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2+sqrt{2({2cos²4θ})}}}

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2+2cos4θ}}

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2(1+cos4θ)}}

⇒ sqrt{2+sqrt{2(2cos²2θ)}}

⇒ sqrt{2+2cos2θ}

⇒ sqrt{2 (1+cos2θ)}

⇒ sqrt{2 (2cos²θ)}

⇒ 2cosθ 

**∴ The required result will be 2cosθ. **

